          "thm-the-l-p-norm-descends-to-the-quotient-and-makes-l-p-a-normed-space",
          "def-multivariate-normal-law"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "statement": "For a finite predictable step process with square-integrable left-endpoint coefficients, every continuous Itô-integral version equals its finite Brownian-increment sum at all times on one measurable probability-one event; on a complete probability space the agreement is indistinguishability. Boundedness of coefficients is not required."
